  (text "KNOBS: RetroSound 258A style controls on RJ9 (4P4C). Contacts 1 black and 4 yellow are ground (shorted inside the knob); 2 red is the encoder (to ground through open / 82k / 30k / 47k, a 2-bit Gray code), 3 green the switches (open; 6.8k outer left; 22k outer right; 0 R push). A reversed phone cord swaps 2 and 3, so both get the same 33k pull-up and 10 nF and go to ADC1: the levels tell the firmware which is which (green 0 / 0.56 / 1.32 / 3.3 V, red 1.57 / 1.94 / 2.35 / 3.3 V)." (at 220 222 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left top)) (uuid "45a1c3e4-3085-57b6-b78d-ee0eecfc4e35"))
  (symbol (lib_id "Connector_Generic:Conn_01x04") (at 240 300 0) (unit 1) (in_bom yes) (on_board yes) (dnp no) (uuid "09491637-7abf-52c9-b733-d33be6cc0be7")
